Z||000016||Racer 1||11-24-1999||03:39 AM||||My tri-Y header bolted right on all you have to do is weld it infront of the cat. Hooker also make a 4 into 1 design but it doesnt have the O2 sensor mount. <A HREF="http://fierorob.homepage.com/DSCengine8.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://fierorob.homepage.com/DSCengine8.JPG</A>  hope this works  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> look up at the top on my website page here the tri-y goes straight out of the head then goes down.<BR> <A HREF="http://fierorob.homepage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://fierorob.homepage.com/</A> <P>||||reg||14
Z||000017||theogre||11-25-1999||12:24 AM||||Monkeyman, you wish windows was half the OS that's on the Macintosh. No I'm not starting a flame........ I use service and make my living of Wintel boxes. I've done so for Mac and Wintel since they wher both invented.<P>Eddies problem is caused very simply by the diferance in keyboards and some inatentive typing. It has nothing to do with the mac. If I moved you from a good IBM or Keytronic keyboard to the cheap slag that has buttons on most systems then you'd likely have the same problem. same problem moving from a cheap KB to a good one.<P>I only use IBM PC-AT & PS/2 style keyboards at home. I've put them on every machine but my girlfriends Compaq. If I use her machine, or one of the ones at work with diferant KB's I have to nearly relearn how to push even one button. allot of the stuff they push for keyboards these days should be trashed. Even some of the "ergonomic" ones bite. Yeah they are a bit more comfortable but they are built out of the same crud.||||reg||1
